From: The gVisor Authors <gvisor-dev@googlegroups.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:45:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kk: enable primitive restart only for indexed draws

In src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c, kk_draw copies
dyn->ia.primitive_restart_enable into data->restart for every draw.
When a non-indexed draw enters the unroll path for flat shading, the
compute kernel compares each vertex number against data->restart_index.
A new command buffer leaves primitive_restart_index at 0 until an index
buffer binds, so the draw drops vertex 0.

Gate data->restart on data->indexed so primitive restart applies only to
indexed draws. First bad upstream commit: 1388ec1b7 ("kk: Support
VK_EXT_provoking_vertex", 2026-08-05).

License: MIT
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
index 8f627aa..04f3494 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_draw.c
@@ -2061,7 +2061,7 @@ kk_draw(struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct kk_draw_command *data)
 
    kk_flush_gfx_state(cmd);
 
-   data->restart = dyn->ia.primitive_restart_enable;
+   data->restart = data->indexed && dyn->ia.primitive_restart_enable;
    data->restart_index = dyn->ia.primitive_restart_index;
    data->flatshade_first =
       dyn->rs.provoking_vertex == VK_PROVOKING_VERTEX_MODE_FIRST_VERTEX_EXT;
